  "limitations": [
    "The GPIO interrupt registration routine and the libgcc __ctzsi2 helper execute in an emulator over authored controller structs, authored MMIO banks and an authored 16-row callback table. No hardware GPIO pin, interrupt or commit acknowledgement is delivered.",
    "The configuration gate 0x80d341d8, the scheduler-state reader 0x80d362b0 and the critical save/restore wrappers 0x80d379ee/0x80d37a1a are supplied return stubs, covered elsewhere. The commit handshake on 0x900080b0 reads authored memory, so no real acknowledgement latency is modeled.",
    "The five trigger modes map to three controller bits (0x34/0x38/0x3c); the edge/level/polarity meaning of each bit, the physical pin roles and the real interrupt delivery remain unproved."
